<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     COMMON MISTAKES
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="content-section" aria-labelledby="mistakes-heading">
  <h2 id="mistakes-heading">Common Mistakes When Converting MEST to EST</h2>
  
  <article style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
    <h3 style="font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif; font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--text);">Mistake 1: Confusing MEST with Standard Central European Time (CET)</h3>
    <p style="color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.7;">
      MEST is European summer daylight saving time (UTC+2). Standard winter Central European Time (CET) is UTC+1. Treating summer time as CET leads to a 1-hour error.
    </p>
  </article>

  <article style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
    <h3 style="font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif; font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--text);">Mistake 2: Forgetting Differing US and EU DST Change Dates</h3>
    <p style="color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.7;">
      Europe changes to summer time on the last Sunday of March, while the US switches to Daylight Saving Time on the second Sunday of March. During these gap weeks, offset math shifts by one hour.
    </p>
  </article>

  <article style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
    <h3 style="font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif; font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--text);">Mistake 3: Date Boundary Miscalculations for Overnight Flights</h3>
    <p style="color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.7;">
      Early morning MEST timestamps (e.g. 2:00 AM MEST Tuesday) convert to 7:00 PM EST on Monday evening. Always check calendar date rollbacks when converting early hours.
    </p>
  </article>
</section>

